-- title:
--   Reducedness of the fibre of a smooth algebra at a maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative rings and let $B$ be an $A$-algebra which is both formally smooth over $A$ (in the sense of `Algebra.FormallySmooth`, i.e. infinitesimal lifting of $A$-algebra maps along nilpotent extensions) and of finite presentation over $A$. Let $I$ be an ideal of $A$ and assume $I$ is maximal. Then the quotient ring $B / I B$ — formally, the quotient of $B$ by the ideal `Ideal.map (algebraMap A B) I` generated by the image of $I$ in $B$ — is reduced, that is, it has no nonzero nilpotent elements. Both rings are taken in the smallest universe; the hypotheses on $A \to B$ together amount to smoothness of $A \to B$, and the conclusion is the reducedness of the fibre of $\operatorname{Spec} B \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ over the closed point $I$, as a ring-theoretic statement about $B \otimes_A A/I$.
--
--   This is the standard fact that the fibres of a smooth morphism over a point with residue field $k$ are reduced (EGA IV 17.5.1), specialised to an affine smooth algebra and a closed point of the base. It is used in the analysis of the blown-up charts of modular curves of full level, in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.blowupChart_primes_transitive_reduced_of_levelAut_stable_of_exceptional_eq_span`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.blowupChart_primes_transitive_reduced_of_levelAut_stable_of_exceptional_eq_span) and its level-one variant, to know that the special fibres occurring there are reduced.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_FormallySmooth_isReduced_quotient_map_of_isMaximal_of_finitePresentation.lean

